{%- comment -%}
  The body of a legal page, taken from the store rather than from the theme.

  Every one of these pages used to carry its own hand-written policy in
  Liquid — several thousand words each, invented at build time, describing a
  business that did not quite match the one in Settings › Policies. The
  merchant maintains the real text in admin, Shopify publishes it at
  /policies/…, and the storefront was quietly contradicting it.

  So the text comes from admin now, and the theme keeps only what it is
  actually for: the hero above, this layout, and the prose styling.

  Params
    policy_body  the admin content to render — shop.<policy>.body for the four
                 Shopify policies, page.content for anything that is a page
                 rather than a policy (the payment policy is one)
    policy_url   where Shopify publishes the same text, used only if there is
                 nothing to render at all

  The table of contents is built by app.js from the headings that arrive,
  because admin HTML has no anchors to link to. It stays hidden until there is
  something in it, so a short policy does not leave an empty rail behind.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign body = policy_body
  if body == blank
    assign body = page.content
  endif
-%}

<section class="section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="legal-layout">
      <aside class="legal-toc" data-legal-toc hidden>
        <h4>On This Page</h4>
      </aside>

      <div class="prose rte" data-legal-body>
        {%- if body != blank -%}
          {{ body }}
        {%- else -%}
          {%- comment -%}
            Nothing in admin and nothing on the page. Better to say so and
            point at the published document than to serve a blank legal page.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <p>This policy is maintained by our team and is being updated.
          {%- if policy_url != blank %} The current version is published at
            <a href="{{ policy_url }}">{{ policy_url }}</a>.{% endif %}
          Please <a href="/pages/contact">contact us</a> if you need it in the meantime.</p>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
